traces.inference_trace:
Scan the array once and remember the index of the previous 1. When a new 1 appears at index `i`, there are `i - prev - 1` zeros between the two 1s. If that count is less than `k`, return false. If the scan finishes without a violation, return true.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    bool kLengthApart(vector<int>& nums, int k) {
        int prev = -1;
        for (int i = 0; i < (int)nums.size(); i++) {
            if (nums[i] == 1) {
                if (prev != -1 && i - prev - 1 < k) return false;
                prev = i;
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
};
```

