The approach is to strip the parentheses, try every split of the digits into a left part and a right part, and build all valid numbers for each part.

For a digit string t, the valid numbers are:
- t itself, if it has no leading zero or is exactly "0".
- t with a decimal point inserted after position i (for i from 1 to len-1), as long as:
  - the integer part t[0..i) is "0" or has no leading zero, and
  - the fractional part t[i..) does not end in '0'.

The integer-part condition means that if t starts with '0' and i > 1, the point is invalid. If t = "0", no point can be inserted because there are no positions.

The fractional part must not end in '0', so the last character of t must not be '0'. If it is '0', only the integer form is possible, and only when t is "0" or has no leading zero.

The case t = "00" gives no valid numbers. Integer form: it has a leading zero and is not "0", so it is invalid. Decimal forms: the integer part "0" is fine, but the fractional part "0" ends in 0, so it is invalid.

Implementation: the content is s.substr(1, n-2). For each split k from 1 to len-1, compute the list for the left part and for the right part, and output "(" + a + ", " + b + ")" for every pair.

The number generator, `gen(t)`:
- If t.size() == 1 or t[0] != '0', add t.
- If t.back() != '0', then for each i in 1..len-1, if i == 1 or t[0] != '0', add t[0..i) + "." + t[i..).

Check with t = "01": t[0] is '0' and the size is 2, so the integer form is skipped. The last character is '1', and i = 1 gives "0.1". Correct.

Check with t = "10": the integer form "10" is added, the last character is '0' so there are no decimals. Correct.

The expected output strings in the examples have trailing spaces, but that is a formatting artifact of the statement, so I produce the standard format without them.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<string> gen(const string& t) {
        vector<string> r;
        int n = t.size();
        if (n == 1 || t[0] != '0') r.push_back(t);
        if (t.back() != '0') {
            for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
                if (i == 1 || t[0] != '0') {
                    r.push_back(t.substr(0, i) + "." + t.substr(i));
                }
            }
        }
        return r;
    }
    vector<string> ambiguousCoordinates(string s) {
        string c = s.substr(1, s.size() - 2);
        vector<string> res;
        int n = c.size();
        for (int k = 1; k < n; k++) {
            vector<string> a = gen(c.substr(0, k));
            if (a.empty()) continue;
            vector<string> b = gen(c.substr(k));
            for (auto& x : a)
                for (auto& y : b)
                    res.push_back("(" + x + ", " + y + ")");
        }
        return res;
    }
};
```

