traces.inference_trace:
Two strings are close exactly when they use the same set of characters and their sorted frequency lists are equal.

1. If the lengths differ, return false.
2. Count the frequency of each of the 26 letters in both strings.
3. For each letter, check that it appears in both strings or in neither. If it appears in only one, return false.
4. Sort the two count arrays and compare them. If they match, return true.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    bool closeStrings(string word1, string word2) {
        if (word1.size() != word2.size()) return false;
        vector<int> a(26, 0), b(26, 0);
        for (char c : word1) a[c - 'a']++;
        for (char c : word2) b[c - 'a']++;
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            if ((a[i] == 0) != (b[i] == 0)) return false;
        }
        sort(a.begin(), a.end());
        sort(b.begin(), b.end());
        return a == b;
    }
};
```

