Track `cnt[x]`, the number of occurrences of each value, and `freq[c]`, the number of distinct values that occur exactly `c` times. Also keep `maxf`, the largest occurrence count seen so far. After processing a prefix of length `i` (1-indexed), the prefix is valid if one of these holds:

1. `maxf == 1`: every value appears once, so removing any one element leaves all counts equal (or the prefix becomes empty).
2. `freq[maxf] * maxf == i - 1`: exactly one element is left over beyond the values with count `maxf`. That leftover must be a value with count 1, so removing it works. This covers the case where all other values have count `maxf` and one value appears once.
3. `freq[maxf-1] * (maxf-1) + maxf == i` and `freq[maxf] == 1`: one value has count `maxf` and all the rest have count `maxf-1`. Removing one occurrence of the top value equalizes them.

Checking case 3 more carefully: the total is `maxf + freq[maxf-1]*(maxf-1)`. If `maxf-1 == 0`, then `freq[0]` would need to be 0, but case 1 already handles `maxf == 1`. For `maxf >= 2`, `freq[maxf-1]` counts only values with exactly `maxf-1` occurrences, and `freq[maxf] == 1` accounts for the single top value. The sum equals `i` exactly when there are no other values.

Case 2 check: with `freq[maxf]*maxf == i-1`, the remaining single element is a value with count 1. If `maxf == 1`, this is case 1 again. If `maxf > 1`, the leftover is one element, so it is a distinct value with count 1, and removing it is valid.

For each prefix where a condition holds, set `ans = i`.

Update order for each element `x`:
- Decrement `freq[cnt[x]]` if `cnt[x] > 0`.
- Increment `cnt[x]`.
- Increment `freq[cnt[x]]`.
- Set `maxf = max(maxf, cnt[x])`.

Array sizes are 100001+.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int maxEqualFreq(vector<int>& nums) {
        vector<int> cnt(100002, 0), freq(100002, 0);
        int maxf = 0, ans = 0;
        for (int idx = 0; idx < (int)nums.size(); idx++) {
            int x = nums[idx];
            int i = idx + 1;
            if (cnt[x] > 0) freq[cnt[x]]--;
            cnt[x]++;
            freq[cnt[x]]++;
            maxf = max(maxf, cnt[x]);
            bool ok = false;
            if (maxf == 1) ok = true;
            else if (freq[maxf] * maxf == i - 1) ok = true;
            else if (freq[maxf] == 1 && freq[maxf - 1] * (maxf - 1) + maxf == i) ok = true;
            if (ok) ans = i;
        }
        return ans;
    }
};
```

