traces.inference_trace:
Greedy approach: keep two pointers, `lo = 0` and `hi = n`. For each character, if it is `'I'`, place `lo` and increment it, so the next value is guaranteed to be larger. If it is `'D'`, place `hi` and decrement it, so the next value is guaranteed to be smaller. After processing all `n` characters, `lo == hi`, and that last value fills the final position.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> diStringMatch(string s) {
        int n = s.size();
        int lo = 0, hi = n;
        vector<int> res;
        res.reserve(n + 1);
        for (char c : s) {
            if (c == 'I') res.push_back(lo++);
            else res.push_back(hi--);
        }
        res.push_back(lo);
        return res;
    }
};
```

