traces.inference_trace:
Build a hash map from each key to its value. Then scan `s` once. Characters outside brackets are copied to the result. On `(`, read up to the matching `)` to get the key, look it up, and append either the value or `?`.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    string evaluate(string s, vector<vector<string>>& knowledge) {
        unordered_map<string, string> m;
        for (auto &k : knowledge) m[k[0]] = k[1];
        string res;
        int n = s.size();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (s[i] == '(') {
                int j = i + 1;
                while (j < n && s[j] != ')') j++;
                string key = s.substr(i + 1, j - i - 1);
                auto it = m.find(key);
                if (it != m.end()) res += it->second;
                else res += '?';
                i = j;
            } else {
                res += s[i];
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
};
```

