traces.inference_trace:
Mark every index within distance `k` of each position `j` where `nums[j] == key`, then collect the marked indices in increasing order. With `n <= 1000`, this is fast enough. To keep it linear, I track the next unmarked index so each index is added at most once.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> findKDistantIndices(vector<int>& nums, int key, int k) {
        int n = nums.size();
        vector<int> res;
        int next = 0;
        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            if (nums[j] == key) {
                int lo = max(next, j - k);
                int hi = min(n - 1, j + k);
                for (int i = lo; i <= hi; i++) res.push_back(i);
                next = max(next, hi + 1);
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
};
```

