traces.inference_trace:
Binary search on the running time T. A time T is feasible if the sum of min(b, T) over all batteries is at least n·T. A battery larger than T can contribute at most T, since it cannot run two computers at once.

The upper bound is sum/n, which is at most about 1e14/1 = 1e14. For the check, sum of min(b, T) is at most 1e5·1e9 = 1e14, and n·T is at most 1e5·1e14 = 1e19, which overflows a signed long long (max about 9.2e18). To be safe, I use the bound hi = sum/n. Then n·T ≤ sum ≤ 1e14, so there is no overflow.

Search lo = 0, hi = sum/n, and take the largest feasible mid, using mid = (lo + hi + 1)/2.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    long long maxRunTime(int n, vector<int>& batteries) {
        long long sum = 0;
        for (int b : batteries) sum += b;
        long long lo = 0, hi = sum / n;
        while (lo < hi) {
            long long mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2;
            long long tot = 0;
            for (int b : batteries) tot += min<long long>(b, mid);
            if (tot >= mid * n) lo = mid;
            else hi = mid - 1;
        }
        return lo;
    }
};
```

