Use prefix sums for rows, columns, and both diagonals, then check each candidate square in O(k).

Let m and n be at most 50. Define:
- `row[i][j]`: sum of row i over columns 0..j-1.
- `col[i][j]`: sum of column j over rows 0..i-1.
- `d1[i][j]`: sum along the main diagonal direction, ending at cell (i-1, j-1), so `d1[i][j] = d1[i-1][j-1] + g[i-1][j-1]`.
- `d2[i][j]`: sum along the anti-diagonal direction, `d2[i][j] = d2[i-1][j+1] + g[i-1][j-1]`, with 1-indexed columns and an array of width n+2.

For each k from min(m, n) down to 2, and each top-left corner (i, j) (0-indexed), do the following:
- The target sum is the sum of the first row: `row[i+1][j+k] - row[i+1][j]`.
- The main diagonal sum is `d1[i+k][j+k] - d1[i][j]`.
- The anti-diagonal runs from (i, j+k-1) to (i+k-1, j). With 1-indexed cells, `d2[r][c]` covers the cell (r, c) and continues up and to the right. The bottom-left cell is (i+k, j+1) and the cell just before the top-right is (i, j+k+1). So the sum is `d2[i+k][j+1] - d2[i][j+k+1]`.
- Check that the diagonals equal the target, then that every row and column in the square equals the target.

If a valid square is found, return k. Otherwise return 1.

For `d2`, the array has width n+2, and `d2[i][j]` for j from 1..n uses `d2[i-1][j+1]`, which is index at most n+1, so it is in range and zero when out of the grid.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int largestMagicSquare(vector<vector<int>>& grid) {
        int m = grid.size(), n = grid[0].size();
        vector<vector<long long>> row(m + 2, vector<long long>(n + 2, 0)),
            col(m + 2, vector<long long>(n + 2, 0)),
            d1(m + 2, vector<long long>(n + 3, 0)),
            d2(m + 2, vector<long long>(n + 3, 0));
        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                int v = grid[i - 1][j - 1];
                row[i][j] = row[i][j - 1] + v;
                col[i][j] = col[i - 1][j] + v;
                d1[i][j] = d1[i - 1][j - 1] + v;
                d2[i][j] = d2[i - 1][j + 1] + v;
            }
        }
        for (int k = min(m, n); k >= 2; k--) {
            for (int i = 0; i + k <= m; i++) {
                for (int j = 0; j + k <= n; j++) {
                    long long t = row[i + 1][j + k] - row[i + 1][j];
                    if (d1[i + k][j + k] - d1[i][j] != t) continue;
                    if (d2[i + k][j + 1] - d2[i][j + k + 1] != t) continue;
