traces.inference_trace:
Mark the broken letters in a boolean array, then scan `text` once, tracking whether the current word contains a broken letter.

- Keep a counter and a flag `ok`, initially true.
- On a space, count the word if `ok` is true, then reset `ok` to true.
- On a letter, set `ok` to false if that letter is broken.
- After the loop, count the last word if `ok` is true.

The examples show trailing spaces (e.g. "hello world "), so the input may end with a space. Counting at every space and again at the end would then count an extra empty word. To handle this, I track whether the current word is non-empty (`len > 0`) and only count words with `len > 0`. Spaces in `brokenLetters` are ignored, since I only mark characters from 'a' to 'z'.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int canBeTypedWords(string text, string brokenLetters) {
        bool broken[26] = {false};
        for (char c : brokenLetters) if (c >= 'a' && c <= 'z') broken[c - 'a'] = true;
        int count = 0, len = 0;
        bool ok = true;
        for (char c : text) {
            if (c == ' ') {
                if (len > 0 && ok) count++;
                ok = true;
                len = 0;
            } else {
                len++;
                if (c >= 'a' && c <= 'z' && broken[c - 'a']) ok = false;
            }
        }
        if (len > 0 && ok) count++;
        return count;
    }
};
```

