This is the classic problem of choosing n non-adjacent elements from a circular array of 3n elements with maximum sum.

To handle the circle, solve the linear version twice: once on slices[0..m-2] (excluding the last) and once on slices[1..m-1] (excluding the first). Take the maximum of the two.

For the linear version, let dp[i][j] be the best sum using the first i elements with j chosen and no two adjacent. Then dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i-2][j-1] + a[i-1]).

Use dp of size (len+1) x (n+1), initialized to 0 for j=0. Unreachable states need care: with i elements you can pick at most ceil(i/2) items. Initialize everything to a large negative value except dp[i][0] = 0, and for i=1 handle dp[i-2] as index 0 (dp[-1] treated as row 0).

Implementation: in the helper, for i from 1..len and j from 1..n, take dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j], and if i>=2 compare with dp[i-2][j-1] + a[i-1]. If i==1 and j==1, compare with a[0]. The row 0 has dp[0][0]=0 and the rest are negative. Row 1 has dp[1][0]=0, dp[1][1]=a[0].

The final answer is dp[len][n]. For the case slices.size()==3 (n=1), each linear array has length 2 and picks 1, which is fine. For size 1 or 2, the constraints say 3n, so the minimum size is 3.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int helper(vector<int>& a, int n) {
        int len = a.size();
        const int NEG = -1000000000;
        vector<vector<int>> dp(len + 1, vector<int>(n + 1, NEG));
        for (int i = 0; i <= len; i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= len; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
                int best = dp[i-1][j];
                int prev;
                if (i >= 2) prev = dp[i-2][j-1];
                else prev = (j == 1) ? 0 : NEG;
                if (prev > NEG) best = max(best, prev + a[i-1]);
                dp[i][j] = best;
            }
        }
        return dp[len][n];
    }
    int maxSizeSlices(vector<int>& slices) {
        int m = slices.size();
        int n = m / 3;
        vector<int> a(slices.begin(), slices.end() - 1);
        vector<int> b(slices.begin() + 1, slices.end());
        return max(helper(a, n), helper(b, n));
    }
};
```

