traces.inference_trace:
Scan the string while tracking how many opening brackets are currently unmatched. Each `'['` adds one. Each `']'` matches an open bracket if one exists, and otherwise counts as an unmatched closing bracket.

Let `u` be the number of unmatched closing brackets at the end. Swapping an unmatched `']'` with an unmatched `'['` fixes two unmatched brackets at once, so the answer is `(u + 1) / 2`.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int minSwaps(string s) {
        int open = 0, un = 0;
        for (char c : s) {
            if (c == '[') open++;
            else {
                if (open > 0) open--;
                else un++;
            }
        }
        return (un + 1) / 2;
    }
};
```

