traces.inference_trace:
Use a monotonic stack of indices and iterate over the array twice (indices 0 to 2n-1, taking `i % n`).

For each position, while the stack is non-empty and the element at the top index is smaller than the current value, pop it and set its answer to the current value. During the first pass (`i < n`), push the current index. Any index left on the stack at the end keeps the default answer of -1.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> nextGreaterElements(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        vector<int> res(n, -1);
        vector<int> st;
        for (int i = 0; i < 2 * n; i++) {
            int v = nums[i % n];
            while (!st.empty() && nums[st.back()] < v) {
                res[st.back()] = v;
                st.pop_back();
            }
            if (i < n) st.push_back(i);
        }
        return res;
    }
};
```

