Track the robot's position as a pair of counters, `x` for horizontal and `y` for vertical. Each `R` adds 1 to `x`, each `L` subtracts 1, each `U` adds 1 to `y`, and each `D` subtracts 1. The robot is back at the origin exactly when both counters are zero after all moves.

The examples show a trailing space in the input (`"UD "`). The loop only reacts to the four valid letters, so any other character is ignored.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    bool judgeCircle(string moves) {
        int x = 0, y = 0;
        for (char c : moves) {
            if (c == 'U') y++;
            else if (c == 'D') y--;
            else if (c == 'L') x--;
            else if (c == 'R') x++;
        }
        return x == 0 && y == 0;
    }
};
```

