Split each cell into 4 triangles (0 = top, 1 = right, 2 = bottom, 3 = left) and merge them with union-find.

Within a cell:
- A blank space joins all four triangles.
- `/` joins top with left (0 and 3) and right with bottom (1 and 2).
- `\` joins top with right (0 and 1) and left with bottom (3 and 2).

Between cells:
- The bottom triangle (2) of cell (i,j) joins the top triangle (0) of cell (i+1,j).
- The right triangle (1) of cell (i,j) joins the left triangle (3) of cell (i,j+1).

The answer is the number of connected components. The index of triangle k in cell (i,j) is (i*n+j)*4+k.

