traces.inference_trace:
The approach is to give each letter a single integer weight and then search for a digit assignment that makes the weighted sum zero.

**Weights.** For each word, the letter at position i from the right gets +10^i. For the result, it gets −10^i. A letter's weight is the sum of these contributions across all words and the result. The equation holds exactly when the sum of weight × digit over all letters is 0.

**Leading zeros.** Mark the first letter of every word and of the result as nonzero. The examples contain trailing spaces (e.g. "SEND "), but the real input won't. To be safe, I skip any non-letter characters. A single-letter word may be 0, since "no leading zeros" only applies to multi-digit numbers. I'll mark the first letter as nonzero only when the word's length (letters only) is greater than 1.

**Search.** Collect the distinct letters, at most 10. Run a DFS over letters, trying each unused digit and skipping 0 for letters marked nonzero. At the end, check whether the running sum is 0. There are at most 10! ≈ 3.6M leaves, which is fine.

**Implementation details.**
- Use `long long` for weights and the running sum.
- Use an index array that maps each letter to its position in the letter list.
- Use a bitmask for the digits already used.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    vector<long long> w;
    vector<bool> nz;
    int n;
    bool dfs(int i, int used, long long sum) {
        if (i == n) return sum == 0;
        for (int d = 0; d < 10; d++) {
            if (used & (1 << d)) continue;
            if (d == 0 && nz[i]) continue;
            if (dfs(i + 1, used | (1 << d), sum + w[i] * d)) return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
    bool isSolvable(vector<string>& words, string result) {
        long long wt[26] = {0};
        bool nzero[26] = {false};
        bool present[26] = {false};
        auto process = [&](const string& s, int sign) {
            string t;
            for (char c : s) if (c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z') t += c;
            long long p = 1;
            for (int i = (int)t.size() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
                wt[t[i] - 'A'] += sign * p;
                present[t[i] - 'A'] = true;
                p *= 10;
            }
            if (t.size() > 1) nzero[t[0] - 'A'] = true;
        };
        for (auto& s : words) process(s, 1);
        process(result, -1);
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            if (present[i]) {
                w.push_back(wt[i]);
                nz.push_back(nzero[i]);
            }
        }
        n = w.size();
        if (n > 10) return false;
        return dfs(0, 0, 0);
    }
};
```

